rgent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in the plan whether removing the `if not key` guard in `signature_findings` intentionally changes foreign-clone op-cert behavior, and update the validate.py docstring (lines 77-79) that still claims a no-op 'When this environment has no key'.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Current guard: `if not key:  # _NO_KEY: nothing to certify against here.` then `return out` (validate.py:91-92)","Plan: 'drop the signing_key read at :87-92 and key=key at :123-124'","Docstring claim now stale: 'When this environment has no key (read-only / foreign clone) the check no-ops rather than flagging everything foreign' (validate.py:77-79)","verify_opcert_record can still return foreign_key (_opcert_verify.py:282,293,308), which the loop appends as a MINOR finding (validate.py:134-141)"],"finding":"Dropping the `if not key: return out` guard in `signature_findings` is a sound way to no-op for HMAC-only stores, but it silently changes behavior for OP-CERT records in a key-less/foreign-clone environment: previously the whole function short-circuited when no HMAC key was present; after removal it will verify op-cert records and can emit `foreign_key` findings where it previously emitted nothing. The function's docstring (validate.py:77-79) still asserts it no-ops 'When this environment has no key', which becomes false.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9fd2e48d4aa1c6ad","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 / src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py:77-92","norm_id":"n4afdcc11f5ceddcf","priority":0.9,"reason":"hig